#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/scripts

# The whole site. Owns the transport and nothing else: each domain is detached
# and brings its own routes, so this file never learns what a thread or a board
# is.
#
# Order matters twice over.
#
# The LANDING PAGE is added first. HttpServer::ResolvePath walks typed children
# in the order they were added and takes the first match, and chess_web.etcs's
# own board_page also answers "/" -- so whichever is attached first owns it.
# Adding landing here, before either lobby is detached, is what makes that
# deterministic rather than a function of which script ran first.
#
# The lobbies are detached AFTER Start. Each one spawns `web` by that same name,
# and spawn_entity retargets a pending name already bound to a live entity of
# the same module and tag -- PersistentNames is process-scope, not per-script --
# so they find THIS server instead of minting a second one and failing to bind
# 8080. Their own Start calls are no-ops: StartConcrete returns false when a
# manager already exists. Their duplicate FileHtmlPage children are harmless
# for the same first-match reason, just redundant.

NetworkProvider
HttpServer web
spawn web
SetPort 8080

web.add(StaticHtmlPage landing)
SetHtmlFromFile ./www/static/index.html
context NetworkProvider::HttpServer web

# Everything else is disk layout as url layout: /chess.html, /forum.html,
# /whitepaper.html. One page type, no per-document entity, and adding a
# document is copying a file rather than editing this script.
web.add(FileHtmlPage tree)
LoadFromDisk ./www
ListPaths tree
context NetworkProvider::HttpServer web

Start
IsStarted

detach chess_lobby.etcs
detach forum_lobby.etcs

# http://localhost:8080/
